            <ArticleTitle>Age-related EBV positive clonal B-cell Lymphoid proliferation (EBV+-DLBCL).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e163-e166</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4317/jced.53314</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Ebstein Barr virus(EBV), herpes virus 5 has been associated with lymphoproliferative disordrers. Age-related EBV+ B-LPD is defined as an EBV+ clonal B-cell lymphoid proliferation or EBV+-DLBCL developing in patients over the age of 40 years in the absence of any known immunodeficiency and without an underlying T-cell lymphoma1. We present a case of EBV+ clonal B-cell lymphoid proliferation. Key words:Oral mucosa ulcer, EBV+-DLBCL, age related.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
